    "Clear VB Decompiler's internal decompilation buffers. DESTRUCTIVE: this discards every existing decompilation result, so the analyzed file must be re-analyzed (re-opened) before the vbd_read_* tools return data again. Use only when implementing a custom full decompilation workflow.": null,
    "Replace a function's code. Pass the function BODY only - without the \"Private Sub ...\" line and without the trailing \"End Sub\"; VB Decompiler adds that wrapper itself. A wrapper present in the input is stripped automatically and the response reports how many lines were removed (stripped_lines). To edit an existing function, read it with vbd_read_function and write back its \"code\" field (NOT \"code_fast\", which contains the wrapper - writing that back would duplicate it). Pass include_previous=\"1\" to get the previous code back for rollback.": null,
    "Set the text of the currently active code window. Automatically calls UpdateAll. Note: the host may normalize what you write, so read-back is not always byte-identical - keep your own copy of important content. include_previous=\"1\" returns the previous text for rollback.": null
